# Third-party notices for the d3 port

Port of d3 to Rust by Carlos (with AI assistance).

This file lists every ported source file in `crates/d3/src/`, the
JavaScript (or other upstream source) it was translated from, which is
vendored under `crates/d3/reference/`, and the licence that applies to
that source. It is the per-file counterpart of `crates/d3/LICENSE` and
`crates/d3/LICENSE.d3-packages`'s gathered notices, and follows the
per-component attribution approach used by the Chromium/WebView
project: every ported file is named, with its original licence and
the path of the file in this repository.

The ported crate itself is `crates/d3` (Rust crate `d3`, version 0.1.0),
a translation of Mike Bostock's d3, version 5.16.0. All d3 packages
are BSD 3-Clause unless noted; the exceptions are:

- `d3-scale-chromatic`: also carries ColorBrewer colour schemes under
  the Apache License, Version 2.0 (Cynthia Brewer, Mark Harrower,
  The Pennsylvania State University).
- `d3-voronoi`: also carries Raymond Hill's Javascript-Voronoi under
  the MIT License.
- `crates/d3/src/ieee754.rs`: translated from V8's
  `src/base/ieee754.cc`, which is adapted from fdlibm by Sun
  Microsystems, Inc.

